                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Note: I'm playing on a Rift CV1 with Xbox controller, and I'm 99% sure Steam is under-reporting my played time by half.\n\nMy first couple of tries with this game at the default perspective and controller settings were pretty frustrating- I was endlessly crashing into trees and hillsides and the controls simply did not do what I was expecting them to do. But once I tried switching into 1st person perspective (X button on Xbox controller) it was immediately clear that I simply needed to invert pitch in my controller settings, and I've been hooked ever since.\n\nThe Hover Jets are much easier to get the hang of and the ring attack matches are lots of fun. I've spent the most time on the Jump Seat levels though, because they're quite a bit more challenging and also pretty addictive.\n\nI enjoy the music and retro graphics, and am looking forward to more environments/tracks and hopefully multiplayer in future updates.\n\nI experienced a bit of VR sickness when I was attempting to play in 3rd person mode (my jet, and thus the camera was constantly tumbling), but when I switch to 1st person things are much better. Still get little gusts of it when my jump seat takes a tumble or when I'm turning on two vectors at once- but it's manageable.\n\nThis is indeed an early access game and it's not entirely polished or glitch free (some inaccurate in-game text, some misplaced foliage in levels, game crashes or hangs if you take of your rift while it's paused), but the overall gameplay is pretty solid.\n\nI've seen some folks wishing for a non-VR version of this game, but I'm here to tell you: You wanna play it in VR. Once you try a seamless flight experience like this in a Rift or Vive, you won't wanna go back to flat-screen gaming.",
